{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "event_id": "fc328c52-36fc-4fb3-815c-dd8eedc26960", "run_id": "R001", "seq": 4, "ts": "2026-09-17T20:00:34.295Z", "type": "prompt", "actor": "human", "phase": "constitution", "condition": "sdd", "task_id": "T-SPLIT-01", "session_id": "48e47389-28d1-4ea5-b4ff-b2a499e9a707", "payload": {"text": "/speckit-constitution Establish the constitution for a small command-line tool project. Principles: (1) Standard library only - no third-party runtime dependencies; (2) Exact money arithmetic - all monetary values handled as integer cents, never floats, and no operation may lose or invent money; (3) Fail loudly - malformed input produces a clear message on stderr and a non-zero exit code, never a silent wrong answer; (4) Every requirement is testable - each functional requirement maps to at least one automated pytest test; (5) Deterministic output - the same input always produces byte-identical output.", "chars": 609, "words": 92, "sha256": "cdc8e975215593fa31a798e584b2c74c5e75ba1c6a3e78c9790d359f47ca7f4d", "source": "hook"}}
